members.member:

Get the accel time for a given axis.

The axis to get the accel time for.
The desired accel time.

See ReturnCode enumeration for info on return codes.

@code
// Get the acceleration time for axis 1 and store it as accel_time.
returnCode = m_skin.axis.GetAccelTime(Skinning.Axes.AXIS_1, out double accel_time);
@endcode


Set the acceleration time for the given axis.

The axis to set the acceleration time for.
The time to set.
See ReturnCode documentation for more info on return codes.
@code
// Set the Accel Time for Axis 1 to a value of .7
returnCode = m_skin.axis.SetAccelTime(Skinning.Axes.AXIS_1, .7);
@endcode


Gets the counts per unit for the given axis.
Warning: Function is Deprecated

The axis to get
The counts per unit for that axis.
See ReturnCode enum for more information about return codes.
@code
// Get the counts per unit for Axis 1 and store it as counts_per_units.
returnCode = m_skin.axis.GetCountsPerUnit(Skinning.Axes.AXIS_1, out double counts_per_unit);
@endcode


Get the deadstart velocity for a given axis.

The axis to get the deadstart velocity for.
The deadstart velocity for that axis.
See ReturnCode enum for more information.
@code
// Get the deadstart velocity for Axis 1 and store in as deadstart_velocity.
returnCode = m_skin.axis.GetDeadstartVelocity(Skinning.Axes.AXIS_1, out double deadstart_velocity);
@endcode


Set the deadstart velocity for the given axis.

The axis to set the deadstart velocity for.
The velocity to set.
SUCCESS if the deadstart velocity was set successfully; ERROR code otherwise.
@code
// Set the Dead Start Velocity of Axis 1 to a value of .2.
returnCode = m_skin.axis.SetDeadstartVelocity(Skinning.Axes.AXIS_1, .2);
@endcode


Get the delta vmax for the specified axis.

The desired axis
The delta vmax for that axis.
SUCCESS or an error code.
@code
// Get the Delta V Max for Axis 1 and store it as delta_v_max.
returnCode = m_skin.axis.GetDeltaVMax(Skinning.Axes.AXIS_1, out double delta_v_max);
@endcode


Set the delta vmax for the specified axis.

The desired axis
The desired delta vmax
SUCCESS or an error code.
@code
// Set the Delta V Max of Axis 1 to a value of 1.3.
returnCode = m_skin.axis.SetDeltaVMax(Skinning.Axes.AXIS_1, 1.3);
@endcode


Get rate for a given axis

The axis to get the rate for.
Either max, slow jog, fast jog minus, or fast jog plus
The rate for the axis.
SUCCESS or an error code.
@code
// Get the Slow Jog Rate for Axis 1 and store it as rate.
returnCode = m_skin.axis.GetRate(Skinning.Axes.AXIS_1, Skinning.Axis.JogRate.SLOW_JOG, out double rate);
@endcode


Get the label for the given axis.

The axis whose label to get.
The label of the axis
SUCESS or an error code.
@code
// Get the Label for Axis 1 and store it as label.
returnCode = m_skin.axis.GetLabel(Skinning.Axes.AXIS_1, out char label);
@endcode


Get the lash comp for an axis.

The axis to get the lash comp for
The lash comp of the axis.
SUCCESS or an error code.
@code
// Get the Lash Comp for Axis 1 and store it as lash_comp.
returnCode = m_skin.axis.GetLashComp(Skinning.Axes.AXIS_1, out double lash_comp);
@endcode


Get the screw pitch for an axis.

The axis to get the screw pitch for
The screw pitch of the axis.
SUCCESS or an error code.
@code
// Get the Screw Pitch for Axis 1 and store it as screw_pitch.
returnCode = m_skin.axis.GetScrewPitch(Skinning.Axes.AXIS_1, out double screw_pitch);
@endcode


Set the label for a given axis.

The axis to set.
The desired label
SUCCESS or an error code.
@code
// Set the Label of Axis 1 to A.
returnCode = m_skin.axis.SetLabel(Skinning.Axes.AXIS_1, 'A');
@endcode


Set the lash comp for a given axis.

The axis to set.
The desired lash comp
SUCCESS or an error code.
@code
// Set the Lash Comp of Axis 1 to a value of .23.
returnCode = m_skin.axis.SetLashComp(Skinning.Axes.AXIS_1, .23);
@endcode


Set the desired rate for the given axis.

The axis to set
The desired rate
Either max, slow jog, fast jog minus, or fast jog plus
SUCCESS or error code.
@code
// Set the Slow Jog Rate of Axis 1 to a value of 3.2.
returnCode = m_skin.axis.SetRate(Skinning.Axes.AXIS_1, 3.2, Skinning.Axis.JogRate.SLOW_JOG);
@endcode


Set the screw pitch for a given axis.

The axis to set.
Give in turns/inch if your machine is in inches; if the machine is in metric, give in mm/turn
SUCCESS or an error code.
@code
// Set the Screw Pitch of Axis 1 to a value of 3.6.
returnCode = m_skin.axis.SetScrewPitch(Skinning.Axes.AXIS_1, 3.6);
@endcode


Get the CSR angle for the CURRENTLY ACTIVE WCS.

The csr angle for the currently active wcs.
SUCCESS or an error code.
@code
// Get the CSR Angle for the currently active WCS and store it as angle.
returnCode = m_skin.csr.GetAngle(out double angle);
@endcode


Get the CSR angle for the specified WCS.

The WCS (1 - 18) whose CSR angle will be returned.
The csr angle for the specified wcs.
SUCCESS or an error code.
@code
// Get the CSR Angle of WCS 6 and store it as csr_angle.
returnCode = m_skin.csr.GetAngle(6, out double csr_angle);
@endcode


Attempt to set the CSR angle for the ACTIVE WCS.

The CSR angle to assign to the active wcs.
SUCCESS or an error code.
@code
// Set the CSR Angle of the currently active WCS to 35.6.
returnCode = m_skin.csr.SetAngle(35.6);
@endcode


Attempt to set the CSR angle for the specified WCS.

The WCS whose CSR angle you wish to set.
The CSR angle to assign to wcs.
SUCCESS or an error code.
@code
// Set the CSR Angle of WCS 7 to 72.3.
returnCode = m_skin.csr.SetAngle(7, 72.3);
@endcode


Get the value of a machine parameter or user variable.

The number of the machine parameter to get (0-999) or user variable (29000 - 34999)
The value of said machine parameter or user variable
SUCCESS or an error code.
@code
// Get the value for machine parameter 32 and store it as myParamValue.
returnCode = m_skin.parameter.GetMachineParameterValue(32, out double myParamValue);
@endcode
Note: the reading of user variables 29000-34999 can occur in any job run state or in any menu.


Sets machine parameter to a given value.

The parameter number 0-999 or user variable 29000-34999
The value to write to the parameter or user variable
true if the parameter was set; false otherwise
@code 
// Set machine parameter 32 to a value of 1.
returnCode = m_skin.parameter.SetMachineParameter(32, 1);
@endcode
Note: the writing of user variables 29000-34999 can occur in any job run state or in any menu.
